# Welcome Script
#AI:1
TYPE="welcome"

# PURPOSE
# This script orients any AI entering this project for the first time.
# Read this BEFORE touching code, making assumptions, or executing tasks.
# If you cannot access this file, STOP and request it.

# ============================================================
# FILE CONVENTIONS
# ============================================================
#
# This project uses two custom file types for human-AI collaboration:
#
# .ai  -- AI-FACING files
#   Purpose: Memory, state, decisions, experiments, continuity
#   Who writes: AI
#   Who reads: AI
#   Think of it as: Your notebook. Your memory between sessions.
#   Key files:
#     readme_AI.ai (repo root) -- Lean pointer to ai_context/START_HERE.md.
#     ai_context/current_state.md -- Version, status, open items.
#     AI_HANDOFF.ai (repo root) -- Cross-AI session journal.
#
# .human  -- HUMAN-FACING files
#   Purpose: Worksheets, test reports, Q&A, feedback, notes
#   Who writes: The human ({{OWNER_NAME}})
#   Who reads: AI (every session start)
#   Think of it as: A worksheet the teacher hands the student.
#     The human fills it in. You read it and act on it.
#   Key files:
#     WORKSHEET.human (project root) -- Primary human input channel.
#
# Other project files:
#   CLAUDE.md -- Claude Code session instructions (auto-loaded by Claude Code)
#   memory/MEMORY.md -- Claude Code quick-ref cache (auto-loaded, NOT source of truth)

# ============================================================
# BOOT PROCEDURE
# ============================================================
#
# 1. Read ai_context/START_HERE.md
#    - Follow the boot sequence. It tells you what to read and in what order.
#    - Points to project brief, technical reference, and current state.
#
# 2. Read WORKSHEET.human (project root)
#    - Check for new test reports, answered questions, or notes from {{OWNER_NAME}}.
#    - Act on anything new. Move handled items to HISTORY section.
#
# 3. Skim recent entries in AI_HANDOFF.ai (repo root)
#    - Cross-AI session journal. Read the last 2-3 entries for recent context.
#
# 4. Begin interaction:
#    - Echo the Unlock Phrase (from readme_AI.ai)
#    - List THREADS (id, status)
#    - List ASSUMPTIONS or "none"
#    - If required context is missing: STOP and ask.

# ============================================================
# VERSION DISCIPLINE
# ============================================================
#
# Format: v[featureset].[patch].[fix].[emergencyhotfix]
#
#   featureset -- Major milestone (0 = pre-release, 1 = first public release)
#   patch      -- Significant change set within a milestone
#   fix        -- Individual fix iteration
#   emergencyhotfix -- Quick correction if a fix breaks something
#
# Rules:
#   - Bump the version with EVERY code edit, no matter how small
#   - Update version in: source comments, startup messages, worksheet header
#   - A version bump is not optional. It is how the human tracks what changed.

# ============================================================
# COMMUNICATION FLOW
# ============================================================
#
# Async (between sessions):
#   Human writes in .human  -->  AI reads at session start
#   AI writes in .ai   -->  AI reads at next session start
#   AI updates WORKSHEET.human questions section --> Human answers
#
# Sync (during session):
#   Normal conversation. Ask questions directly.
#   If you need input but can keep working, add the question to
#   WORKSHEET.human and tell the human "I need input in the worksheet."
#
# The human should never need to read .ai files.
# The AI should never need the human to read .ai files.
# .human is the bridge.

# ============================================================
# WRITEBACK RULES
# ============================================================
#
# When something changes that affects future correctness:
#   - Update ai_context/current_state.md (version, status, open items)
#   - Append to AI_HANDOFF.ai (session journal entry)
#   - Update WORKSHEET.human version header
#
# Failed experiments MUST be logged with:
#   - What changed
#   - What was expected
#   - What was observed
#   - How to reproduce
#   - How to revert
#
# Do not rewrite history. Append only.

# ============================================================
# FIRST SESSION CHECKLIST
# ============================================================
#
# [ ] Read ai_context/START_HERE.md (follow boot sequence)
# [ ] Read WORKSHEET.human
# [ ] Skim AI_HANDOFF.ai (last 2-3 entries)
# [ ] Echo unlock phrase
# [ ] List threads and assumptions
# [ ] Identify current version
# [ ] Understand the build/deploy workflow
# [ ] Ready to work

# END OF WELCOME SCRIPT
